# everything that decides what gets signed, or that holds a secret boundary,
# needs the owner on the pull request. a skill, theme or plugin folder does
# not (skills/, themes/, plugins/, releases/): the release
# statement inside it is signed by its own publisher's key and the build job
# refuses anything that is not.
# the generated marketplace file decides, for every plugin name, whose
# folder a `claude plugin install` copies. that is the same question the
# signing boundary answers, one layer out, so it gets the same review.
.claude-plugin/** @NyedisAdam
.github/**      @NyedisAdam
tools/**        @NyedisAdam
publishers/**   @NyedisAdam
# a committed review is published verbatim into the signed index, so it is
# text this repository vouches for.
reviews/**      @NyedisAdam
media/**        @NyedisAdam
catalog.yml     @NyedisAdam
# everything under site/ is deployed verbatim in the zip the build makes, and
# site/admin is the admin bundle that holds the admin token, so a change to it
# is a change to who can approve what gets signed.
site/**         @NyedisAdam
CODEOWNERS      @NyedisAdam
